            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of continuous paravertebral and extradural infusions of bupivacaine for pain relief after thoracotomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>204-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain was controlled in 20 post-thoracotomy patients using a continuous infusion of 0.25% bupivacaine through an extradural or para-vertebral catheter. Both techniques provided good analgesia. Hypotension and urine retention occurred significantly less frequently in the paravertebral than in the extradural group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
